From 47c71220f554d9f84f24fadd52eb53d86705b6df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:19:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5KGW1P sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver for the Samsung S5KGW1P, a 64MP CMOS image
sensor on a 3-trio MIPI CSI-2 C-PHY interface. It is the main camera of
the Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

The driver exposes a 2x2-binned 4624x3468 mode at 30 fps and a 4x4-binned
2000x1128 mode up to 120 fps with exposure, analogue/digital gain, flip,
vblank/hblank and test-pattern controls. The register tables were decoded
from the vendor CamX sensor module. The chip-id read is retried on
power-up because the sensor intermittently NAKs the first I2C access.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
